## Memory Management Architecture
A three-tier memory system handles pattern storage and evolution:

1. Short-Term Memory (STM)
- Temporary pattern storage
- Initial coherence validation
- Quick pattern access and modification

2. Medium-Term Memory (MTM) 
- Patterns promoted from STM based on coherence (>0.7)
- Pattern relationship tracking
- Stability assessment

3. Long-Term Memory (LTM)
- Stable patterns with high coherence (>0.9)
- Deep pattern relationships
- Historical evolution tracking

